From 8a1d4772ad541bbba8adbdf11843828361f9330e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Somalapuram Amaranath <somalapuram@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:25:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/nouveau: skip fbdev client setup on a card with no
 CRTCs

Second, independent guard for the same oops. Clearing DRIVER_ATOMIC in
nouveau_display_create() should be sufficient on its own, and the disassembly
agrees on the mechanism -- drm_atomic_commit+0xbe is the return address of

    mov 0x2f8(%r14),%rax     ; dev->mode_config.funcs
    mov 0x20(%rax),%r11      ; ->atomic_commit
    call *%r11

so ->atomic_commit really is NULL, which only happens when no display was
created and nouveau_mode_config_funcs (.fb_create and nothing else) is still
installed. That is exactly the case the first guard tests for. The panic
nevertheless reproduced, so this does not depend on any capability bit being
right: an fbdev console needs a CRTC to scan out to, a card with none has
nothing to set up, and drm_client_setup() is simply not called for it.

Costs nothing real -- there is no console to lose on a card with no CRTC, and
earlier boots of the affected laptop already said as much:

    nouveau ...: [drm] No compatible format found
    nouveau ...: [drm] Cannot find any crtc or sizes

Both guards now log when they fire, so the next boot says which path was taken
instead of leaving it to be inferred:

    nouveau ...: no atomic_commit installed; DRIVER_ATOMIC cleared
    nouveau ...: no CRTCs; skipping fbdev client setup

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GyZRNL2xBh9BWrNiQX2Hsh
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c |  4 ++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c     | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
index 22fcf3a373b3..4f881ece88e5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_display.c
@@ -735,8 +735,10 @@ nouveau_display_create(struct drm_device *dev)
 	 * (drm_drv.h:532), so clearing it here disables atomic for this card only
 	 * and leaves a second, display-capable nouveau card untouched.
 	 */
-	if (!dev->mode_config.funcs->atomic_commit)
+	if (!dev->mode_config.funcs->atomic_commit) {
 		dev->driver_features &= ~DRIVER_ATOMIC;
+		NV_INFO(drm, "no atomic_commit installed; DRIVER_ATOMIC cleared\n");
+	}
 
 	drm_mode_config_reset(dev);
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
index e16f59b00f6f..f5dfe3e99442 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_drm.c
@@ -901,7 +901,39 @@ static int nouveau_drm_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 	else
 		format = NULL;
 
-	drm_client_setup(drm->dev, format);
+	/* An fbdev console needs somewhere to scan out. A card with no CRTCs has
+	 * nowhere, and setting the client up anyway is what oopses this driver on
+	 * a hybrid laptop: the discrete GPU there is a 3D controller with no
+	 * display outputs, and earlier boots said so plainly --
+	 *
+	 *     nouveau ...: [drm] No compatible format found
+	 *     nouveau ...: [drm] Cannot find any crtc or sizes
+	 *
+	 * With nouveau.atomic=1 that same path stops being merely useless and
+	 * becomes fatal, because drm_client_modeset_commit() then takes the atomic
+	 * branch into drm_atomic_commit(), whose last act is an indirect call
+	 * through dev->mode_config.funcs->atomic_commit. On a card that never
+	 * created a display that pointer is NULL -- nouveau_mode_config_funcs
+	 * (nouveau_display.c:353) defines .fb_create and nothing else -- so the
+	 * kernel jumps to 0 during probe, before anything is mounted:
+	 *
+	 *     drm_atomic_commit+0xbe/0xe0        <- return addr of "call *%r11"
+	 *     drm_client_modeset_commit_atomic+0x19b/0x230
+	 *     drm_fbdev_client_hotplug+0x66/0xb0
+	 *     nouveau_drm_probe+0x15d/0x170
+	 *     RIP: 0010:0x0
+	 *
+	 * nouveau_display_create() already clears DRIVER_ATOMIC for such a device,
+	 * which should be enough on its own; this is the second, independent guard,
+	 * and the one that does not depend on any capability bit being right.
+	 * Skipping it costs nothing real either way -- there is no console to lose
+	 * on a card with no CRTC.
+	 */
+	if (drm->dev->mode_config.num_crtc) {
+		drm_client_setup(drm->dev, format);
+	} else {
+		NV_INFO(drm, "no CRTCs; skipping fbdev client setup\n");
+	}
 
 	quirk_broken_nv_runpm(pdev);
 	return 0;
-- 
